@startuml
title Identity — Refresh Token Rotation

autonumber

actor User
participant "Frontend" as FE
participant "AuthController" as Controller
participant "RefreshTokenService" as Refresh
participant "JwtService" as Jwt
participant "UserRepository" as UserRepo
database "identity DB" as DB

User -> FE : Continue working with expired access token

FE -> Controller : POST /refresh\nrefresh cookie

Controller -> Refresh : rotate(refreshToken)

Refresh -> DB : find refresh token/session
DB --> Refresh : token / not found

alt token exists and is valid

    Refresh -> DB : invalidate old refresh token
    DB --> Refresh : invalidated

    Refresh -> UserRepo : find user
    UserRepo -> DB : SELECT user
    DB --> UserRepo : user
    UserRepo --> Refresh : user

    Refresh -> Jwt : createAccessToken(user)
    Jwt --> Refresh : new access JWT

    Refresh -> Refresh : generate new refresh token
    Refresh -> DB : save new refresh token
    DB --> Refresh : saved

    Refresh --> Controller : access JWT + new refresh token

    Controller --> FE : 200 OK\nnew access JWT\nSet-Cookie: new refresh

else token expired / revoked / invalid
    Refresh --> Controller : refresh rejected
    Controller --> FE : 401 Unauthorized\nClear refresh cookie
end

note right of Refresh
Rotation rule:

old refresh token -> invalid
new refresh token -> active

A previously used refresh token
must not remain valid.
end note

@enduml
